# A crossup pushes the defender away from where the attacker stands, not the way the attacker faces. p1's forward
# jump passes p2 on frame 37 and its j.C, still facing right (nobody turns in the air), hits p2 from behind on
# frame 38. Once the hitstop (11) ends p2 slides left, away from p1; pushed the way p1 faces, it would slide right,
# through p1.
setup: p1 character testman
setup: p2 character testman
setup: p1 x = -75500
setup: p2 x = 70000

frames 1-5: p1 9
frame 31: p1 5c                          # j.C, active on frames 38-42

frame 37: expect p1 x = 73000            # past p2
frame 38: expect p1 event hit
frame 38: expect p1 facing = right
frame 38: expect p2 facing = right       # toward p1
frames 38-49: expect p2 x = 70000        # hitstop
frame 50: expect p2 x = 68750            # the first slice of the 10000 pushback (1250), to the left
# From frame 51 p1 comes down into p2's pushbox on its right and pushes it further left.
frames 51-70: expect p2 x < 68750
frames 57-70: expect p2 x = 49500
frames 57-70: expect p2 facing = right
frames 60-70: expect p1 x = 119500
